  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food crisis response in Somalia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As in most parts of the Somalia, Gu rains were poor in Gedo region resulting in crop and pasture failure and water scarcity. The price of locally produced foods have doubled and livestock prices have decreased resulting in a poor purchasing power of the population in all the districts of Gedo region. The situation has resulted in outward migration of the rural population to urban areas including Dollow district. In response to the increasing needs, SADO will implement a 2-month cash intervention to assist the most vulnerable drought affected IDP households to receive immediate assistance, and ensure a first-line defense against further deterioration through early response. The transfer value is aligned to Somalia CWGs recommended transfer values for Multi-Purpose Cash Assistance for Gedo region.</narrative>
  </description>
